Description: less-but-smarter terminal log viewer
 zerch is a terminal log viewer with search, filters, highlights,
 bookmarks, and log-level / timestamp awareness. It builds an in-memory
 index (memory-mapping the file and scanning it in parallel), so it opens
 multi-gigabyte files nearly instantly and searches them in well under a
 second.
 .
 The --view string captures the full view (filters, highlights, bookmarks,
 revealed ranges, search, selected line) as one compact, shareable token, so
 an exact view can be saved or handed off as a single string.
